    "created_at": "2020-04-26T13:40:52Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-04-26T13:40:52Z",
    "body": "> The various postMessage() APIs are consistent in observable behavior. Performance differences are acceptable.\r\n\r\nAs long as this doesn't result in `self.postMessage()` becoming async as well, this sounds perfectly reasonable to me.\r\n\r\nThat is, I think implementation-specific delays in `postMessage` are perfectly acceptable as long as the message still gets sent and not blocked on the current thread's event loop forever.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
